  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community based literacy, capacity and livelihoods development  (Somaliland)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Unlike the rest of Somalia, Somaliland has enjoyed relative peace and stability for the last 13 years. However, this peace has not produced the level of development expected, and poverty continues to be rife. A key reason is the high rate of illiteracy. This project seeks to address people&apos;s educational and economic needs, and the development of sustainable civil society structures. Central to the project will be the provision of basic education classes for orphans and vulnerable children, and literacy classes for marginalised teenage girls and poor illiterate members of women&apos;s groups. The establishment of community managed resource centres will sustain this development and contribute towards building a culture of self sufficiency amongst the target communities. As a result, more disadvantaged children will enrol and achieve better results in school, and structures will be in place to sustain this over the long term.</narrative>
  </description>
